{{--
  The account-state banner (plan §7.5, §13.5).

  Rendered by the app layout on every screen, above the topbar, when the
  workspace's billing needs attention. Two states and no more, because a
  banner that appears for everything is a banner nobody reads:

    past_due  — a charge failed. Nothing has been taken away; the point of the
                banner is that the customer finds out before the period ends.
                (Set by staff since M5; license renewals are dunned by email
                and by the license's own expiry.)
    at a cap  — an account limit is full (seats, storage, API keys). Only shown
                to the owner, who is the one to ask support for more.
--}}
{{--
  The at-cap state names whichever quotas are full, from `usage.atCap` — the
  same numbers that blocked the create, never a second calculation. Nothing
  here names a quota, so a quota added or removed with a feature needs no edit
  (`start/quotas.ts`, docs/modules.md).

  Plain `&&` rather than `?.` on purpose — Edge's expression parser is a
  subset of JavaScript and no template here relies on optional chaining.
--}}
@let(atCap = usage && usage.atCap ? usage.atCap : [])

@if(organization.status === 'past_due')
  <div class="account-banner account-banner-danger" role="status">
    <span>
      <strong>We could not take payment.</strong>
      Nothing has been switched off yet. Update your card to keep your licenses running.
    </span>
    @if(isOwner && hasRoute('billing.index'))
      <a href="{{ urlFor('billing.index') }}">Update payment method</a>
    @end
  </div>
@elseif(isOwner && atCap.length > 0)
  <div class="account-banner" role="status">
    <span>
      <strong>
        {{ atCap.length > 1
          ? `You are out of ${andList(atCap.map((quota) => quota.noun))}.`
          : `You are using all ${atCap[0].limit} of your ${atCap[0].noun}.` }}
      </strong>
      Everything you have keeps working — only creating something new is blocked.
    </span>
    @if(hasRoute('support.create'))
      <a href="{{ urlFor('support.create') }}">Ask for more</a>
    @end
  </div>
@end
